I really like the idea of sharing bones files.  HOWever, what happened to
me the other night shouldn't happen to a dog, and I gravely fear that that 
bones.8 file which I'd picked up here was to blame.

Marvin the Wizard had had a fairly ho-hum first couple of levels.  On level 3 
he found a nice big general store with loads of scrolls of identify, a blessed 

Orcrist on sale at an extortionate price, an uncursed amulet of esp (which he
turned out not to need after an eye floated through the door...), _and_ 
uncursed rings both of polymorph and of polymorph control; so, after eating 
and drinking his fill, Marvin the Xorn walked out through the walls and over
to the stairs.  The next several levels were good clean fun (I've never been
a Xorn before).  I found Giantslayer, made Sting just for good measure,
cleaned out a throne room (though the throne vanished in a puff of logic),
got into trouble once but teleported away (the scroll was cursed and took me
back to the shop: no problem--just a chance to pick up a few more bargains), 
and was soon on dungeon level 7, going down the stairs to level 8.  

.. And the next thing I knew, I was back at the DOS prompt, reading the 
message EOF ON FILE 8.

Anyone know what happened?  I'm playing the same patch level as the bones 
donor, also on a PC; I had uudecoded the file and to my untutored eye it 
looked fine.  Was the whole thing a coincidence?

